cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "ExtremoNet: cross-species network analysis of Deinococcus radiodurans and human stress-defence proteins"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Ananthapadmanabhan"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-03
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ananthapadmanabhan333/Cross-Species-Oxidative-States-"
keywords:
  - protein networks
  - network alignment
  - functional analogy
  - Deinococcus radiodurans
  - oxidative stress
  - DNA repair
  - STRING
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline that builds STRING functional-association networks of the oxidative-stress
  and DNA-repair proteins of Deinococcus radiodurans and Homo sapiens, compares them by topology,
  modules and IsoRank alignment against degree-preserving null models, and ranks every cross-species
  protein pair with a transparent, evidence-graded score that separates orthologs, homologs, distant
  homologs and candidate functional analogues. All results are computational candidates.
